# Commonly confused words: "accept" where "except" (apart from) is meant.
# why: Except means apart from (everyone except Tom). Accept means take or agree to.
expr main [<([everyone, everybody, everything, all, anyone, anybody, nobody, nothing, anything, someone, each, every, none, (all of us), (all of them), day, days, week, weeks] accept [for, the, me, you, him, her, them, us, Tom, when, that, this, those, these, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday, weekends, holidays]), accept>, <(accept for), accept>]

let message "Did you mean `except` (apart from)? `Accept` means to take or agree to."
let description "Fixes `accept` where `except` is meant: `everyone accept Tom` → `everyone except Tom`."
let kind "Malapropism"
let becomes "except"
let strategy "MatchCase"

test "Everyone accept Tom came." "Everyone except Tom came."
test "We are open every day accept Sunday." "We are open every day except Sunday."
test "It was fine accept for the noise." "It was fine except for the noise."

allows "Please accept my apology."
allows "I accept the terms."
allows "Everyone must accept the rules."
